lture"},{"text":"Nursery management"},{"text":"Landscape horticulture"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Modern Production"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Protected cultivation"},{"text":"Hydroponics"},{"text":"Drip irrigation"},{"text":"Fertigation"},{"text":"Climate control"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"Remote sensing"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"IoT"},{"text":"Computer vision"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Business"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Farm economics"},{"text":"Costing"},{"text":"Supply chain"},{"text":"Post-harvest management"},{"text":"Agricultural marketing"}]}]},{"heading":"Ideal Graduate Profile","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A strong Botany graduate targeting Horticulturist should aim to graduate with:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc Botany","practical horticulture training","nursery/greenhouse internship","plant propagation skills","crop production knowledge","plant protection","irrigation/fertigation","post-harvest knowledge","GIS/IoT exposure","data analytics","a practical smart-horticulture project."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Best first-job targets"},{"type":"flow","items":["Horticulture Trainee","Nursery Executive","Farm/Greenhouse Executive","Crop Production Executive","Horticulture Assistant"]},{"type":"p","text":"With experience and/or an M.Sc. specialisation, the graduate can progress toward Horticulturist, Crop Specialist, Nursery Manager, Farm Manager, Protected Cultivation Specialist, Researcher or Horticulture Consultant."}]}]}